      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T10:25:38Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(edm): wire EDM constant taper - posed moves, leaning-kerf verify, max-angle and U/V refusals\n\nA Wire Contour states a signed taper angle (#290 D2): the profile and\nthe #532 laws hold on the top plane at the kerf across the leaning\nwire, each side leans square to itself and the corners along the\nmitre, and every move's pose is the wire's direction toward the upper\nguide. The wire laws (#534) read a stated taper's poses as the wire's\nlean at every judged height (elliptical kerf reach), so a gouge at any\nheight blocks the post; any other posed move stays refused. The\nmachine check judges every lean against edm.max_taper_deg, the guide\nplanes and the U/V strokes; the wire post writes taper_on / uv /\ntaper_off from edm.codes with X Y at the lower guide. Zero taper is\nbyte-identical to the vertical cut.\n\nFixes #536\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
